Under Article 75 of the Saudi Labor Law, an indefinite-term contract may be terminated by either party with written notice to the other. The notice period is 60 days when the worker is paid monthly (the employer's notice to a worker paid monthly is also 60 days), and 30 days for workers paid on other bases. The worker's notice is covered by Article 75(1)? In my understanding, the 60-day period applies to the worker's termination for a monthly-paid worker, and 30 days for the employer's notice, though this should be checked against the current text.

Correction: Article 75 says the party terminating must give 60 days' written notice if the worker is paid monthly, and 30 days otherwise. The employer's notice is 60 days for monthly paid workers and 30 for others. A worker's notice is 30 days for all workers. Article 75 text, as amended, requires the worker to give 30 days' written notice.

